<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $X$ be the mapping simplex of the sequence of functors 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \calE \stackrel{g}{\rightarrow } \calD \stackrel{f}{\rightarrow } \calC . \]
</div>
    <p>
       Since $f$ and $g$ are associated to restrictions of $\calM $, we obtain a commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \times _{\Delta ^2} \Lambda ^2_1 \ar @{^{(}->}[d] \ar [r] &amp;  \calM \ar [d] \\ X \ar [r] \ar @{-->}[ur]^{s} &amp;  \Delta ^2} \]
</div>
    <p>
       The left vertical inclusion is a pushout of $\calE \times \Lambda ^2_1 \subseteq \calE \times \Delta ^2$, which is inner anodyne. Since $p$ is inner anodyne, there exists a dotted arrow $s$ as indicated in the diagram. The restriction $s| X \times _{\Delta ^2} \Delta ^{ \{ 0,2\} }$ exhibits that the functor $f \circ g$ is associated to the correspondence $\calM \times _{\Delta ^2} \Delta ^{ \{ 0,2\} }$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>